{"name":"Phosphorus","hex":"#a5d0c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Phosphorus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A name sometimes used for Hesperus, the personification in Greek mythology of the planet Venus.","An Ancient Greek name for the morning star (the planet Venus when it is visible in the eastern sky before sunrise)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Phosphorus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Phosphorus","blocks":[{"text":"Phosphorus is a chemical element; it has symbol P and atomic number 15. All elemental forms of phosphorus are highly reactive and are therefore never found in nature. Elemental phosphorus can be prepared artificially, the two most common allotropes being white phosphorus and red phosphorus. With 31P as its only stable isotope, phosphorus has an occurrence in Earth's crust of about 0.1%, generally as phosphate rock. A member of the pnictogen family, phosphorus readily forms a wide variety of organic and inorganic compounds, with as its main oxidation states +5, +3 and −3."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Phosphor_rot.jpg/330px-Phosphor_rot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorus","wikidata":"Q674"},{"title":"Phosphorus (morning star)","blocks":[{"text":"Phosphorus is the god of the planet Venus in its appearance as the Morning Star. Another Greek name for the Morning Star is \"Eosphorus\", which means \"dawn-bringer\". The term \"eosphorus\" is sometimes met in English. As an adjective, the word \"phosphorus\" is applied in the sense of \"light-bringing\" and \"torch-bearing\" as an epithet of several gods and goddesses, especially of Hecate but also of Artemis/Diana and Hephaestus. Seasonally, Venus is the \"light bringer\" in the northern hemisphere, appearing most brightly in December, signalling the \"rebirth\" of longer days as winter wanes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Lucifer_%28the_morning_star%29._Engraving_by_G.H._Frezza%2C_1704%2C_Wellcome_V0035916.jpg/330px-Lucifer_%28the_morning_star%29._Engraving_by_G.H._Frezza%2C_1704%2C_Wellcome_V0035916.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorus_(morning_star)","wikidata":"Q1775444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG/500px-Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG/1280px-Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG/500px-Wei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWei%C3%9Fer_Phosphor.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Phosphor-rot-violett.jpg/500px-Phosphor-rot-violett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Phosphor-rot-violett.jpg/500px-Phosphor-rot-violett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhosphor-rot-violett.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Black_Phosphorus_Ampoule.jpg/500px-Black_Phosphorus_Ampoule.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Black_Phosphorus_Ampoule.jpg/1280px-Black_Phosphorus_Ampoule.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Black_Phos